\begin{definition}[Decoder Family and Structural Closure]\label{def:decoder}
A decoder family uses one declared class set and acts on the specified history windows. For each intervention-response comparison, declare its response cells and a matching relation on those cells. The family is structurally closed when decoder class equality composes exactly and the response-cell matching relations are reflexive, symmetric and transitive. These are conditions on the chosen comparison data; they are not inferred from a numerical tolerance alone. The legibility clauses below supply the additional operational requirements.
\end{definition}

