\begin{remark}[Tolerance Alone Is Not Transitive]\label{rem:tolerance-control}
With constant decoder labels, let response matching mean distance at most $1$ on $\{0,3/4,3/2\}$. Adjacent points match, but the endpoints do not. Thus decoder equality plus raw tolerance is not enough. By contrast, equality under a declared response-cell map is an equivalence relation and supplies a concrete structurally closed matching rule. This example concerns closure only, not satisfaction of all six legibility clauses.
\end{remark}

